-- title:
--   A point of order M' whose multiples are cut out by the Γ₀-component
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring and $\ell', M', q$ natural numbers with $M' \neq 0$. Two variable-change stability hypotheses are assumed: first, that for every $A$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every quadruple $D = (x_P, y_P, x_Q, y_Q)$ of elements of $T$, if $(x_P,y_P)$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)$ satisfy the affine equation of $W$, $\mathrm{preΨ}_{\ell'}$ vanishes at $x_P$ and at $x_Q$, and the two elements $\prod_{1 \le a \le (\ell'-1)/2}(x_Q\,\Psi_a^2(x_P) - \Phi_a(x_P))$ and $\prod_{1 \le a \le (\ell'-1)/2}(x_P\,\Psi_a^2(x_Q) - \Phi_a(x_Q))$ are units, then the same holds for $C \bullet W$ and the translated quadruple $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$; second, that the predicate [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55) at $(p,k)$ — for $p^k = 2$: $\deg h \le 1$, $h$ has coefficient $1$ in degree $1$ and $h \mid \Psi_2^2$; otherwise: $\deg h \le \varphi(p^k)/2$, the coefficient of $h$ in degree $\varphi(p^k)/2$ is $1$, $h \cdot \mathrm{preΨ}_{p^{k-1}} \mid \mathrm{preΨ}_{p^k}$, and $h$ divides $W.\mathrm{smulNumerator}\,a\,(\varphi(p^k)/2)\,h$ for all $2 \le a \le (p^k-1)/2$ with $p \nmid a$ — is preserved on passing from $W, h$ to $C \bullet W$ and `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A$-algebras, $\mathcal{T}$ a level transport datum for $\mathcal{G}$ at level $q$, and $\kappa$ an algebraically closed field which is an $A$-algebra with $M' \neq 0$ in $\kappa$. Let $x$ be a raw point over $\kappa$ of the rigid moduli datum `rigidDataPow A ℓ' M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, that is, a Weierstrass curve $x.\mathrm{curve}$ over $\kappa$ with unit discriminant together with level data for the triple product component (a family of polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$, a Katz level-$\ell'$ quadruple, and a Drinfeld level-$q$ pair) satisfying the corresponding level conditions. Then there is a point $g$ of the affine model of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ over $\kappa$ with $\mathrm{ord}(g) = M'$ such that for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and every nonsingular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n \cdot g = (x_1, y_1)$ and $\mathrm{ord}(n \cdot g) = p^{v_p(M')}$, the polynomial $(x.\mathrm{level}.1)\,p$ — the $\Gamma_0$-component of $x$ at $p$ — has $x_1$ as a root.
--
--   This is the existence half of the dictionary between the generator-kernel polynomials of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-component of a rigid Weierstrass level datum and points of exact prime-power order on the curve: the components $(h_p)_{p \mid M'}$ are matched with the $x$-coordinates of the generators of cyclic subgroups whose product is generated by a single point of order $M'$. It is used in the analysis of full-level data on Tate curves and in the associated computations of $j$-invariants and Frobenius reductions.
